acceptance_criteria: Record the exact failed command and verify the current fix or upstream blocker without weakening tracker governance.
repro_steps: "Let the scheduled 'Sync GitHub issues into pm' workflow run on main with the pm-github pin before 2026.11.15; the 11-14, 11-15 and 11-16 scheduled runs failed."
resolution: "Fixed by pinning pm-github 2026.11.15 (#208); proven by scheduled run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/44053423017."
expected_result: "The scheduled sync on main passes the gated import, the repeat-import no-op check, the tracker and changelog gate and strict pm health."
actual_result: "Merged in #208 as 38f8f1e (pm-github 2026.11.15 pin). The first scheduled run on that pin, https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/actions/runs/44053423017 (2026-11-17, main at bfe6297), succeeded at every gated-sync step: gated GitHub to pm import, verify repeat import is a no-op, gate tracker and regenerated changelog, verify strict pm health. Round AC's earlier failure came from a local dry run, not from the scheduled workflow."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T10:46:53.041Z",codex-sol,"Run 43827565812 failed the pm-github 2026.11.4 idempotency gate: one shared provenance tag and one conflicting target. The shared #150 reference belongs to distinct pack-storage and crash-matrix tasks, so neither is a duplicate. pm-github 2026.11.15 separates references from explicit import ownership. Reuse open PR #208 and its caller pin; retain current main and verify the pinned dry-run. No item is closed."
  "2026-11-16T11:02:01.561Z",codex-sol,"Initial review receipt: the failed workflow log and current pin are documented in docs/issue-sync-2026-11-16.md. Seeded tracker validation passes through pm test --run --progress. Typecheck and lint pass. The quick package suite remains running under shared-host load; no complete passing suite is claimed.   Publish review evidence with pending gates explicit; no scheduled success is claimed."
  "2026-11-17T02:02:22.939Z",pi-glm,"Reopened in review round AC: the acceptance dry-run command registered on this item still fails on current main (exit code 1). The gate refuses the import plan as not idempotent - one duplicate provenance tag in the existing corpus and one conflicting target - so the duplicate-provenance repair delivered by PR 208 does not fully clear the scheduled sync's gate. No item was written by the dry run. The follow-up should identify the conflicting target and either repair its provenance tag or deduplicate the corpus entry before the next scheduled sync."
  "2026-11-17T05:25:26.148Z",codex-sol,"PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64PD8_: both test (22) job 133761825088 and test (26) job 133761825369 fail exact-gates operational CLI acceptance because the committed bundle differs in this item, its history and CHANGELOG.md. Both logs name identical paths; uncovered audit/docstring branches occur after that failed assertion. No separate runtime regression found. Regenerating archive after all tracker edits, then committing and verifying accept:self-host and the operational CLI test at HEAD."
  "2026-11-17T05:25:42.869Z",codex-sol,"Targeted gates passed: npm run typecheck; npm run lint; npm run changelog:check; npm run build. Existing acceptance commands are linked for the committed-HEAD verification; full coverage remains CI-owned. The scheduled-sync duplicate-provenance acceptance blocker remains open."
  "2026-11-17T05:30:04.160Z",codex-sol,"Committed-HEAD npm run accept:self-host passed. The operational CLI test timed out on local disk; with supported fast temporary storage it passed self-host acceptance then hit an identity-audit refusal in the shared Git object database. This is separate from both CI failures, which failed earlier on stale archive content. Verify the unchanged operational test from a clean single-branch clone of the final committed HEAD; no allowlist or thresholds are weakened."
